{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem","id":89555,"title":"Dragon Bloods Work Better as a Party than Solars or the Inverse Cleric Problem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-12T10:14:02-07:00","id":89555,"title":"Dragon Bloods Work Better as a Party than Solars or the Inverse Cleric Problem","content":"<br /> <br /> The cleric dilemma in DnD is the mechanical fact that nearly every party needs a cleric, but not every group has a player that wants to play a cleric. Something of an inverse to this occurs in Solar games, but not as much in Dragon Blood games. I think that running Dragons Bloods works better than running Solar circles at the gaming table because the system is set up to favor Solar specialization at the cost of a smooth game whereas Dragon Bloods castes tend to be more balanced against each other. This premised on the notion that players want some equality of table time, or game attention, while playing the game, an idea that I take as granted for the purpose of this first post.<br /> <br /> As people are aware, the current system of rules are quite flawed. The system makes combat, which is probably the most system-heavy activity in the game, way too complicated. The result of this complication is that combat-focused characters and their players receive a greater amount of ST attention than other characters because the combat monkeys\u2019 turns take so damn long to resolve. Furthermore, STs must gear their combat encounters generally towards the higher end of the character spectrum then towards the average character combat competency to ensure that a challenge is actually a challenge to the whole group. While a chain is only as durable as its weakest link, a Solar circle is generally as strong as is toughest Dawn. By itself, this observation is less than remarkable, but these problems are greatly aggregated by the specialization of Solar castes. Solar castes are strongly encouraged to specialize in narrow fields, include combat for the Dawn caste. As a result, Dawn caste characters and their players receive a significant and disproportionate amount of attention both during combat and during the planning of combat encounters. This negatively affects the enjoyment of the players of other castes who either must pay a premium in out of caste charms to be effective (that is, have an effect) in combat, or must endure playing second fiddle to Dawns for much of the game session. Even when the non-Dawn Solar invests in skills and charms sufficent to be a dynamo alone against mortal enemies, which will typically be the case, the non-Dawn is still likely to be a second stringer when fighting supernatural foes, fights that will likely be most of the fights rolled out in the game.<br /> <br /> In contrast to the Solars, Dragon Bloods do not have one particular caste that specializes in combat. Instead, the Dragon Blood castes each have a separate combat skill. Although not all the combat skills are equally effective, throwers are likely to do less damage than close-combat junkies, because no one caste has a total combat focus Dragon Blooded characters are more likely to be in closer pariaty to each other in terms of combat effectiveness. As such, Dragon Blood games are likely to develop a more equal share of table time between different characters and players. Of course there still be combat focused Dragon Blooded who will more effective than other Dragon Blooded but this will be less of a problem both because the Dragon Bloods will not be tied to a particular role by their caste (the \u201ccleric problem\u201d that someone needs to fill a role because the mechanics of the game demand it, rather than because that\u2019s what the player wants his character to do) and because Dragon Blood combat charms develop more slowly than Solar ones. By this latter statement, I mean that DB combat charms do not escalate in power as quickly as Solar ones do and as such a DB journeyman of combat skills will relatively closer in combat ability to a DB master of combat skills than a Solar journeyman would be to a Solar master.<br /> <br /> Because of this, Dragon Blood groups will be better for players because we can expect Dragon Bloods to have greater equality in combat time and therefore play time in general.<br /> <br /> However, the analysis does not end there. As a follow up, it is reasonable to ask if the Solar game can be rehabilitated to ensure greater equality in game time. I submit it can through player education, ST oversight, and the development of a simplified combat system.<br /> <br /> The relationship between character mechanics and resulting table time are not intuitive. Solar players, particularly new Solar players, must understand how their mechanical choices may affect their table time. In so doing, Solar players should realize that the inherent specialization of their castes may have a negative effect on the game itself. Leveraging mechanical advantages in the game may have the unintended result of diminishing the fun in the game. The solution on the player side is for the Solar player to downplay specialization by having non-Dawns become more proficient in combat and Dawns branch out a bit into non-combat skills and such. Avowedly, the goal would not be to ensure that non-Dawns have equal combat proficiency with Dawns, but rather to ensure that non-Dawn characters are simply not totally and completely outshone by their Dawn comrades. If anything, the onus should be placed upon Dawn players to stretch their wings outside their assigned sphere both because the mechanical advantages of specializations are compelling and because the importance of combat will likely be self-evident to non-Dawns but it is possible that Dawns may equally understand why it is important that their characters spread out their abilities. In that regard, the importance of player to player communication in setting up characters cannot be understated because a Dawn player may be understandably wary of expanding into a field covered by another caste. A Dawn player would reasonably be upset if his character expanded into, say, Sail, only to discover that the Eclipse has focused on that.<br /> <br /> Storytellers also play an important role. The Storyteller should carefully govern character creation and development to ensure that the game runs well. I cannot stress enough that this sort of oversight must continue past character creation. It is quite possibly, indeed even likely, that a character\u2019s relative combat table time may not be apparent until several sessions into a campaign.<br /> <br /> One final recommendation is that the combat system should be simplified and streamlined such that combat takes less time. This will free up more time for other aspects of role playing and make the table time of combat less important. As it currently stands, combat takes way, way too long even when there is a parity of combat skills between characters. Obviously the new system is being developed with this in mind.<br /> <br /> This concludes my primary analysis. I am sure a lot of people will point out points that require clarifications or raise alternative ideas.<br /> <br /> As a topic of discussion, I am interested if people have some idea on what proportion of combat charms should be in a Solar\u2019s charm set, particularly at character creation. Is there some way to make a general assessment about what percentage a Dawn\u2019s charm should be combat charms versus a non-Dawn\u2019s percentage of combat charms?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T10:55:20-07:00","id":89576,"title":"","content":"Personally I always found that the Dawns got the ass-end of the ability list. <br /> <br /> Generally speaking, of Archery, Martial Arts, Melee and Thrown you really only need 1. Outside of very specific encounters, you're probably not going to find too many situations of, &quot;Sorry, but you don't have the right Combat Ability so you'll basically be kind of worthless this scene.&quot; <br /> <br /> So the Dawn has 4 combat Abilities, 3 of which are essentially redundant. Then he gets 5 Favored abilities to try and do everything else non-combat related.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the other castes spend one Favored Ability on Melee/Martial Arts/Thrown/Archery, maybe another one on Dodge (allowing them to easily hold their own and compete with the Dawn in most combat situations) and then have plenty of options for non-combat situations. <br /> <br /> When I run Solar games it's very rare for someone to actually want to play a Dawn, simply because the only thing they do well is combat, and even then it's not going to be much better than another Caste who picks up a combat Ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T11:04:34-07:00","id":89581,"title":"","content":"Dragonbloods have another problem, actually - their weird selection of specialties can make it difficult to play one that doesn't focus on the traditional abilities of their caste, and a group of DBs that doesn't have at least 3 of the 5 castes in it will find it hard to do much of anything outside of their skillset. Solars have an easier time developing a broad range of abilities and adapting to new circumstances.<br /> <br /> I can also say from experience as a Dawn with a Martial Arts focus that only being able to punch things can be very restrictive. I spent most of my XP on things not related to my caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T11:15:30-07:00","id":89593,"title":"","content":"The problem of Exalted's rules heavily favoring specialization, while also making unskilled allies a disadvantage in many situations (such as combat, or social interaction) is very real, and so deeply baked-in I am unsure how it could be fixed with anything grown from the many-Ability DNA of the Storyteller System.<br /> <br /> I am not sure that Dragon-Blooded have it less than others. I am sure that the combat monster in most Solar groups I've seen has been a Twilight or a Night. Poor Dawn Caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T11:24:12-07:00","id":89601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=89576#post89576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I run Solar games it's very rare for someone to actually want to play a Dawn, simply because the only thing they do well is combat, and even then it's not going to be much better than another Caste who picks up a combat Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dawn Caste PCs will be more appealing in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T12:04:04-07:00","id":89628,"title":"","content":"I agree with others in this thread, Dawn is the most boring caste in 2e, since you really only need one combat ability and the three others just feel wasted.<br /> <br /> But DBs aren't really much better off because of the 1 mote elemental surcharge on non-aspect charms, which limits what other abilitys you would want to specialize in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2355-ratatosk","name":"Ratatosk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T12:40:39-07:00","id":89643,"title":"","content":"I agree at least that 2E combat is too slow and too likely to bog down on certain characters' turns, but any caste can learn extra action charms. As mentioned, Dawns are saddled with redundant caste abilities on top of an ability, War, that depends on a subsystem that some groups may never use. Until the errata gave Dawns access to certain combat charms, Dawns who wanted to be good at combat had very little choice of which abilities to favor. Overall, I think you've spotted a real problem, but it's one with 2E combat, not the Dawn caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T12:50:32-07:00","id":89649,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, a Dawn Caste is still the supreme king of combat because of the 2.5 Dawn anima - +2 DV and a -1 external penalty is pretty overwhelming. It's just superior in a boring way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T13:42:27-07:00","id":89682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ratatosk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=89628#post89628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with others in this thread, Dawn is the most boring caste in 2e, since you really only need one combat ability and the three others just feel wasted.</div> </div> </div> </div>The focus on just one combat ability is an aggravating factor to the problems I'm discussing. When you focus on one combat ability to the exclusion of others you naturally wind further down the charm tree. That means more and more complicated charms and combos which in turn mean more table time for resolution of the fighter. Indeed, this is more of a problem for Solars because their charms are so much more powerful, both natively and how they grow in power relative to DB charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem of Exalted's rules heavily favoring specialization, while also making unskilled allies a disadvantage in many situations (such as combat, or social interaction) is very real, and so deeply baked-in I am unsure how it could be fixed with anything grown from the many-Ability DNA of the Storyteller System.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think a few solutions are possible. One is to have the ST keep a tight leash on players and character growth. The problem with that is that it robs players of agency over their characters.<br /> <br /> Another is to mollify the issue by reducing the amount of time it takes to resolve dramatic actions, probably by simplifying the rules set. This will, at the least, reduce the amount of table time combat monkeys take up and free up time for other players.<br /> <br /> One final way is to install mechanics gates to slow specialized growth down charm trees. This would most like be accomplished by raising Essence minimums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T14:34:25-07:00","id":89716,"title":"","content":"As a side to the original post, you'll find the screen time/skill investment is proportional to the standard Physical/Social/Mental divide, which is inverse to the net impact on the environment/setting. or in other words, Mental focused character get the least &quot;screen time&quot; but when they do (Craft, sorcery, lore) they have the largest setting impact, making things that destroy cities, casting spells to destroy nations, creating new nations of whole cloth. Where you have the physical which is the opposite, a lot of screen time but killing people one on one while it can be important, doesn't have the same level of impact.<br /> <br /> You see this less in dragonblooded both because, as indicated, they are weaker overall but also because dragonblooded charms in 2e are all built around the same general ideals of killing things. There are some charms for the non-killing things tasks, but they are relatively few. Think about it, think about the iconic charms of Solars. The tiger warrior training, and lore equivalent. Wyld Shaping. Glorious Solar Saber and it's variants in other abilities. You have combat charms there, but there are others. Dragonblooded... Lore? Elemental bolt. The elemental dodge charm... vortex charms that kill everyone around you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T14:54:03-07:00","id":89732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=89601#post89601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dawn Caste PCs will be more appealing in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall hearing something like each Caste will have 7 Caste Abilities, pick 5 of them, then pick 5 more Favored. Is that right? Or did my imagination vomit that up from nowhere?<br /> <br /> If it's true, I think the new Solar List would be enough of a spoiler to keep the Forum busy until the book ships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T15:45:59-07:00","id":89781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=89732#post89732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recall hearing something like each Caste will have 7 Caste Abilities, pick 5 of them, then pick 5 more Favored. Is that right? Or did my imagination vomit that up from nowhere?<br /> <br /> If it's true, I think the new Solar List would be enough of a spoiler to keep the Forum busy until the book ships.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC Someone suggested it a few months back, along with a host of other ideas. One of the devs agreed it was an interesting idea. The fan base pretty much ran with it from there.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'd give it fair thought for a modification to a 2e/2.5e game if I were running one. I do however count myself fortunate that I am not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T15:55:07-07:00","id":89787,"title":"","content":"Our group was talking about this recently, though from a different angle.<br /> <br /> There are 25 Abilities. A single Solar gets to effectively favor* 10 of them. Throw out Abilities that don't apply to your game (Sail, sometimes Survival, sometimes Bureaucracy, etc.) and you're down to about 20-22 Abilities depending on Caste, etc. So right there -- bam! -- a single player is eating up half of the Abilities. Then throw in 3-4 more players and issues with character point-buy optimization theory crafting. Things get tight pretty quickly and the Charm picks become really important at differentiation.<br /> <br /> Then introduce issues like; two players have Judge's Ear Technique, or Lock Opening Touch, or Hypnotic Tongue Technique, or Respect-Commanding Attitude. What do you do now? Take turns activating them and feeling useful?<br /> <br /> Or the opposite problem where you have 4-5 players with widely different competencies. Good luck consistently getting through sessions where everyone feels useful.<br /> <br /> * Sorta. You get where this is going, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/994-heroicantagonist","name":"heroicantagonist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar994_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T16:01:55-07:00","id":89792,"title":"","content":"I think the best way to look at this is to use the basketball team metaphor. Just because you have Michael Jordan on the team doesn't mean the rest of the team sits there with their thumbs up their asses, and good defense and teamwork can carry a team that lacks a reliable star player. It's okay if some people are better at combat than others as long as everybody has something to do and there are distinct roles to be played, not all of which necessarily require a mega-badass. In Legends of the Wulin, I played the weakest fighter in the party and was consistently useful in a support role, with the occasional personal score. Everyone has some baseline combat ability in that game, and I built for the role I wanted to take, but a lot of it was just that the game was designed to support that sort of play, which Exalted traditionally has not.<br /> <br /> One of the things that makes DBs good is that their charm trees tend to have some combat applicability stuck in there regardless of what they are. This was an intentional choice to emphasize their martial bent, but it's a good principle in general for a game where combat and combat ability are taken for granted. I am curious to see if 3e dips its toe in those waters in the Solar charmset. D&amp;D is actually also a good example of this methodology, particularly 4e.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, this is the kind of thing that has to be addressed when you're designing your combat system, because you can only do so much to patch it with powers. If you <i>need</i> to keep 30% of your build choices sunk into combat stuff to remain functional in combat when you're partied up with two combat-heavy characters, that reflects a fundamental issue with the way the game was built.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-12-2014, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T16:05:31-07:00","id":89795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=89781#post89781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Someone suggested it a few months back, along with a host of other ideas. One of the devs agreed it was an interesting idea. The fan base pretty much ran with it from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, interesting. I was so sure. I distinctly recall the &quot;7 Caste Abilities, pick 5&quot; mention/confirmation coming from someone on the EX3 Team, but I'm not sure I want to trust my memory here. I can't find it on the Ex3 Wiki or Nishkirya, at all. Could be that isn't the plan, after all.<br /> <br /> That said, it's a solution that would fit with this comment:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matthew Roark's wife: Your Dawn (and Solars of all castes) will have far more mobility in choosing outside of their classic caste Abilities at chargen, without using up their favored choices. No keywords, no complicated mix and match. It's built right into the chargen rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T16:18:00-07:00","id":89804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BvBPL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=89682#post89682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The focus on just one combat ability is an aggravating factor to the problems I'm discussing. When you focus on one combat ability to the exclusion of others you naturally wind further down the charm tree. That means more and more complicated charms and combos which in turn mean more table time for resolution of the fighter. Indeed, this is more of a problem for Solars because their charms are so much more powerful, both natively and how they grow in power relative to DB charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Focusing on multiple combat abilities is a bit of a trap. Athletics charms give Melee and MA characters the ability to close with enemies, and they also give Thrown and Archery characters the ability to stay far away, so there's no need to do something like Archery + Melee. Doubling up means your character is either mediocre at two combat abilities or is only good at combat, since you've thrown dots and charms and XP at two combat trees instead of just one. Athletics, on the other hand, lets you participate more outside of combat.<br /> <br /> Combos are cool on paper, since you get to come up with clever names, special effects, and so on, but they can also feel like an XP sink that gets in the way of healthy character growth. A character with, say, 10 charms for an ability probably has no use for at least a few of them, making those charms a waste of XP. Then she has to buy a combo to really use them, which could mean another 2-3 charms worth of XP. Even better, she has to decide when to buy the combo. Buying a combo early means having fun with her charms sooner and having a better chance to survive, but it also means paying for a new combo - possibly more than once - after learning more charms. After all that cost, you can bet she'll use her best combo (with a 2-die stunt for WP) every turn.<br /> <br /> The combo system also discourages lower-end investors in combat charms. If a thinker or crafter or social character decides to learn 3 or 4 combat charms eventually, he has to pay more XP to use them decently. After all, he may not have Dex 5, Melee 5 and a Grand Daiklave, so he needs every edge he can get. Also, he's possibly inclined to spread those charm purchases out (after all, combat isn't his focus), making it more likely that he'll need to buy a second combo later to meaningfully use the charms he's just picked up. If you're hoping just to contribute meaningfully in combat, investing so much XP is not a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> If you haven't already, I strongly encourage you to check out the 2.5 errata. The errata don't solve every problem with 2E (combat still takes forever) but they do fix some under- and over-powered charms on top of eliminating combos. At the very least, this means players get to use their XP to grow their characters instead of to buy weak prerequisites or to buy charms they can't use for a few more months until they can afford a new combo. Exalted 2E kind of reminds me of D&amp;D 3.5: if you don't have the time and inclination to learn the whole system and plan your character really well, it's easy to get frustrated and feel like you're overshadowed and progressing more slowly than other people. Both games can be fun for a while, but it gets really tiresome to deal with the large disparities in character power and spotlight time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T16:42:28-07:00","id":89815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=89792#post89792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things that makes DBs good is that their charm trees tend to have some combat applicability stuck in there regardless of what they are. This was an intentional choice to emphasize their martial bent, but it's a good principle in general for a game where combat and combat ability are taken for granted. I am curious to see if 3e dips its toe in those waters in the Solar charmset. D&amp;D is actually also a good example of this methodology, particularly 4e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say DB's elemental thematics (paired with their origin as troops of the Exalted army) give much more creative leeway here than Solar's perfection.<br /> <br /> Still, it's worth noting that even in 2e, every Solar Caste has something in it's Ability spread that can be utilized for combat:<br /> Zenith: Resistance, Integrity, Holy attack Charm in Presence<br /> Twilight: Spirit-Cutting, extra temporary HLs in Medicine, Sorcery<br /> Night: Dodge (duh), Athletics (mobility and even a damage enhancer), Stealth (properly utilized it's completely devastating in 2e/2.5 combat)<br /> Eclipse: Ride and Sail both have their combat uses, though admittedly, they're clearly the least militant caste.<br /> <br /> There isn't much support for using those Abilities as combat enhancers in their Charms, but the premise is there and can be expanded upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T21:51:29-07:00","id":89930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=89815#post89815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stealth (properly utilized it's completely devastating in 2e/2.5 combat)</div> </div> </div> </div>I always see this, and... yes, if you're fighting things not designed with knowledge of the combat system. It's basically useless if you're fighting anything with a surprise negator though, which means <i>every enemy the ST wants to matter</i>. Turning your Stealth to near-irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":261,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","user":"notthepenguins","date":". 03-13-2014, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T21:55:41-07:00","id":89932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=89716#post89716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side to the original post, you'll find the screen time/skill investment is proportional to the standard Physical/Social/Mental divide, which is inverse to the net impact on the environment/setting. or in other words, Mental focused character get the least &quot;screen time&quot; but when they do (Craft, sorcery, lore) they have the largest setting impact, making things that destroy cities, casting spells to destroy nations, creating new nations of whole cloth. Where you have the physical which is the opposite, a lot of screen time but killing people one on one while it can be important, doesn't have the same level of impact.<br /> <br /> &lt;snip&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, in Modern terms:<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Sports figures (Football, Baseball, Basketball, etc), Soldier<br /> <b>Social:</b> Actors, Activist, Politicians<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Scientists, Hackers<br /> <br /> While there may be some crossover, and there has been <i>(An actor as a President? A Wrestler as a Governor?)</i>, for the most part they don't. Sports Figures -- and even Soldiers as a group -- get a lot of &quot;Screen Time&quot;, along with Actors, Activists &amp; Politicians. Not so much for the Scientists &amp; Hackers. When it comes to the physical side of things, the Sports Figures &amp; Soldiers excel, but when a good movie or some social injustice need to be fought, well in comes the Actors and the Activists...and of course, the Politicians subtly &quot;Rule the Day&quot; while they get an inordinate amount of &quot;Screen Time.&quot; And behind it all, hidden in their Laboratories, are the Scientists, without whom none of today's modern miracles would be possible -- yet they get little thanks. Of course, the Hackers take full advantage of that technology...for whatever purpose they want to put it to -- to right injustices, to make money, or to bring down nations!<br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">P.S.: I am, in no way, saying that &quot;Soldiers&quot; (or any of the above) are Socially or Mentally inept (or Physically, in the case of the others). I've known many &quot;Soldiers&quot;...and am a retired one myself. This is just an example...ok? Just wanted to clarify, before anyone got their &quot;knickers&quot; in an uproar.</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":2141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","user":"Nadrakas","date":". 03-13-2014, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T01:02:16-07:00","id":90026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=89930#post89930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=89815#post89815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stealth (properly utilized it's completely devastating in 2e/2.5 combat)</div> </div> </div> </div>I always see this, and... yes, if you're fighting things not designed with knowledge of the combat system. It's basically useless if you're fighting anything with a surprise negator though, which means <i>every enemy the ST wants to matter</i>. Turning your Stealth to near-irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's a problem that hopefully won't make a reappearance in 3e. Still, the principle of a stealthy character using his stealth to gain a combat advantage is pretty sound and works in many different systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T01:16:29-07:00","id":90032,"title":"","content":"As to the OP:<br /> I actually find Solars work better as a party together than Dragonblood, most of the time. Not for reasons of power or skillset, but for fluff reasons. The Solars have to work together because of the Wyld Hunt, plot, etc, and also because they're so rare they're the only ones who have things in common with each other, and often end up making friends with each other. There's generally no particular reason why they should not like each other, unless they come from diametrically opposed cultures.<br /> Whereas in most Dragonblood games (though not all) the PCs are Dynasts from different houses. And those houses often spy on each other, compete, clash, and if you're running the Civil War (which I imagine is in a fair few DB games) they could end up on opposite sides, which makes the PCs clash. I've never had a Solar or Lunar killed or driven from the party by another party member, I have had DBs killed, or driven out of the party, by other party members.<br /> And more generally, most of the Celestial parties I've seen, while not everyone always has got on, have been a lot better at working together than the DB parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T01:51:27-07:00","id":90051,"title":"","content":"True that, Wizard. The enemy of my enemy might not necessarily be my friend, but he's at LEAST a potentially useful tactical asset.<br /> <br /> Also: working together as a party isn't about power levels so much as personalities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T02:04:33-07:00","id":90057,"title":"","content":"Dawns having the capacity for a greater diversity of Abilities is probably really helpful, but it's my expectation that between their new threefold Anima and the desire to give each combat Ability a distinct tactical profile, they really will shine in combat.<br /> <br /> I mean, just think about what the capacity afforded by &quot;early buy in gives you significant expertise&quot; is there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T03:21:15-07:00","id":90078,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I get the impression in 3rd ed that it'll be more appealing to want to have a wide variety of combat styles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90051#post90051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: working together as a party isn't about power levels so much as personalities.</div> </div> </div> </div> I certainly find that. Personality, beliefs, background and method of getting things done are, in my experience, the main things that cause parties to work together or not.<br /> <br /> I've never seen difference in charms and abilities to be a big issue.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T04:23:10-07:00","id":90091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90078#post90078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I get the impression in 3rd ed that it'll be more appealing to want to have a wide variety of combat styles.<br /> <br /> I certainly find that. Personality, beliefs, background and method of getting things done are, in my experience, the main things that cause parties to work together or not.<br /> <br /> I've never seen difference in charms and abilities to be a big issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, save in particularly egregious circumstances of power difference. Also certain specific sets of Charms, occasionally--it could be REALLY hard to work with a practitioner of Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style in 2e, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T04:59:15-07:00","id":90108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90032#post90032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the OP:<br /> I actually find Solars work better as a party together than Dragonblood, most of the time. Not for reasons of power or skillset, but for fluff reasons. The Solars have to work together because of the Wyld Hunt, plot, etc, and also because they're so rare they're the only ones who have things in common with each other, and often end up making friends with each other. There's generally no particular reason why they should not like each other, unless they come from diametrically opposed cultures.<br /> Whereas in most Dragonblood games (though not all) the PCs are Dynasts from different houses. And those houses often spy on each other, compete, clash, and if you're running the Civil War (which I imagine is in a fair few DB games) they could end up on opposite sides, which makes the PCs clash. I've never had a Solar or Lunar killed or driven from the party by another party member, I have had DBs killed, or driven out of the party, by other party members.<br /> And more generally, most of the Celestial parties I've seen, while not everyone always has got on, have been a lot better at working together than the DB parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangentially, it's quite fascinating how so many groups have it easier to assemble a ragtag band of murderhobos from bumfuck nowhere into a party than create a group of peers sharing common background in a highly organized, very social culture. I've seen that problem come up with both versions of Vampire, as well as Legend of the Five Rings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T08:00:06-07:00","id":90224,"title":"","content":"Part of that stems from the fact that the society you describe, especially L5R, has very specific expectations of duties from each of the different houses and clans, which many times do not mesh well, or at all, with others. F'rex, it's very difficult to come up with a reason for a Lion, Unicorn, Scorpion, Dragon, and Mantis to work together in anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T08:32:22-07:00","id":90235,"title":"","content":"And with Vampire, I think the main issue is that most Vampires are horrible people, caught up in vicious politics, and members of competing clans (though I noticed it varied by clan, in the LARP I played, the Nosferatu could just turn up and they'd immediately become friends and form an informal coterie, but most of the rest of the clans were pretty dysfunctional).<br /> <br /> Which is essentially the issue with Dynastic games as well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-13-2014, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T10:44:51-07:00","id":90334,"title":"","content":"It would work if everyone was from the same house, but it's hard enough to get everyone to play the same splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T12:07:14-07:00","id":90367,"title":"","content":"This is why in my Dragonblooded games I've tried to encourage a view of the Great Houses as overwhelmingly interconnected, every Dynast PC having close relatives in other houses, tried to push push political factions into cross-house conspiracies, and tried to suggest that due to the often vast differences in age between members of a family with Dragon-Blooded members, the most revered kinship in Realm society isn't that between parents and offspring, between siblings or even between spouses, it's between members of a Sworn Brotherhood. You can't choose your ancestors, and your mate may be a political necessity out of your control, but your Brotherhood is your truest family.<br /> <br /> This is harder when a faction leader is also a house elder like Mnemon, and pretty much demands that Dynastic Charms be flushed. But it has let me encourage PCs to treat Brotherhood goals as higher priorities than House goals, and to let inter-party conflicts reach a sharper more familial pitch without spilling over to PC deathmatches. In my Creation, the most tragic figure in Realm literature is the last faithful soldier who continues to cherish the ideals of a Sworn Brotherhood that split up over some conflict too monumental to endure (and the most common cause of such conflicts is the reason there's a subtle taboo against Brotherhood members becoming lovers). On the other hand, the last living soldier in a Brotherhood that <i>died fighting</i> is treated as a paragon of Dragon-Blooded virtue, with a duty to educate the rising terrestrial generation. Joining or forming a new Brotherhood is certainly an option for a sole survivor, but it's one that comes with a lot of complicated baggage. While there's a lot of social pressure on young Dragon-Blooded to join into Brotherhoods, a lone survivor is generally permitted to endure in stoic solitude if they prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T15:50:45-07:00","id":90461,"title":"","content":"DB spoilers hot from the playtest<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded have no charms since they're not, you know, real exalted. All of their capabilities have been modeled as techniques and are tiered as such, power-wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T18:12:32-07:00","id":90532,"title":"","content":"Seems fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would work if everyone was from the same house, but it's hard enough to get everyone to play the same splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do allied houses to an extent. Ie Cynis, Mnemon and Sesus are all very tight. But people probably aren't going to want to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T19:05:17-07:00","id":90556,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90108#post90108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentially, it's quite fascinating how so many groups have it easier to assemble a ragtag band of murderhobos from bumfuck nowhere into a party than create a group of peers sharing common background in a highly organized, very social culture. I've seen that problem come up with both versions of Vampire, as well as Legend of the Five Rings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because GMs and players do not regularly sit down during character development and work together to make a cohesive backstory. As much as nearly every RPG book says it is a great idea to do just that, it is very rare. <br /> <br /> Generally speaking, it isn't necessarily a bad thing to be a band of thugs brought together by happenstance. I mean, that's the Italian Job or the Sting right there. Plenty of fertile ground for a game. <br /> <br /> Most systems have their player character mechanics gates to ensure that there's a standard power level for each character. This standardization of power means that it is more permissible for characters to come up with characters in a vacuum, rather than as part of a cooperative experience, because it ensures that one character will not significantly outshine another. <br /> <br /> However with Solar Exalted, it is quite possible to develop a character, right from the get-go, that mechanically far and away surpasses other PCs. In fact, it is incredibly easy and even likely that a Dawn will be created exactly like that because that's the path of least resistance in creating a Dawn. This underscores the importance of the players and ST working together to create a balanced Solar party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T00:50:39-07:00","id":90725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BvBPL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90556#post90556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's because GMs and players do not regularly sit down during character development and work together to make a cohesive backstory. As much as nearly every RPG book says it is a great idea to do just that, it is very rare.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, it isn't necessarily a bad thing to be a band of thugs brought together by happenstance. I mean, that's the Italian Job or the Sting right there. Plenty of fertile ground for a game.<br /> <br /> Most systems have their player character mechanics gates to ensure that there's a standard power level for each character. This standardization of power means that it is more permissible for characters to come up with characters in a vacuum, rather than as part of a cooperative experience, because it ensures that one character will not significantly outshine another.<br /> <br /> However with Solar Exalted, it is quite possible to develop a character, right from the get-go, that mechanically far and away surpasses other PCs. In fact, it is incredibly easy and even likely that a Dawn will be created exactly like that because that's the path of least resistance in creating a Dawn. This underscores the importance of the players and ST working together to create a balanced Solar party.</div> </div> </div> </div>This obviously varies a lot group to group. None of the people I play with ever create characters in isolation; group character creation will often take a full session or two before we start actual play. Sometime character concepts will be hashed out for weeks before play starts.<br /> <br /> And there's an inherent implication in this whole thread that combat is a significant portion of play time. I have been in sessions of Exalted where no combat occurred at all.<br /> <br /> I think the bigger problem is really that 2e is so bad of a system that if you play it the way being implied - isolated character creation, frequent combats - you're left in a situation where, unless absolutely everyone has close to perfect system mastery, there are a billion traps to fall into in terms of creating wide power gaps, and those power gaps will matter excessively, because anytime combat happens it's going to take forever to resolve.<br /> <br /> Thing is, 2e's combat is a reason not to play 2e, even before the other issues come into play. So the problems that arise mostly because of that combat system aren't an issue with one splat over another... they're an issue with 2e combat effectively making it so that you don't really have room to do anything else if combat is happening with any frequency. When you solve the resolution time issue, either by using a less obnoxious system or by having relatively few combat situations, almost all of the concerns you were expressing go away, at least, in the hands of a halfway competent ST.<br /> <br /> There is very little accounting for bad STs in any of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T01:55:09-07:00","id":90747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90032#post90032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never had a Solar or Lunar killed or driven from the party by another party member, I have had DBs killed, or driven out of the party, by other party members.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might have helped if you didn't love your treachery so much... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But more seriously, if it's the game I'm thinking of, it's worth noting that the original party (ten years ago) worked together reasonably well, though that may have been because they spent an extended period in the Threshold when they weren't that powerful and wound up learning to work together and bonding over shared secrets (like what we did to Sesus Lahore). The main barrier to getting the group to bond organically is having characters who are powerful enough to be moderately self-sufficient and/or being in a position where you can rely on your House to pull you out of the fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90032#post90032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And more generally, most of the Celestial parties I've seen, while not everyone always has got on, have been a lot better at working together than the DB parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't match my experience when running Celestials games from scratch (unlike the current one where I'm the second GM to run it); IME it's often like herding cats until you get a couple of players who are on the same wavelength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":978,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","user":"Iozz-Sothoth","date":". 03-14-2014, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T02:13:36-07:00","id":90756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iozz-Sothoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90747#post90747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But more seriously, if it's the game I'm thinking of, it's worth noting that the original party (ten years ago) worked together reasonably well, though that may have been because they spent an extended period in the Threshold when they weren't that powerful and wound up learning to work together and bonding over shared secrets</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough, but by the time I started playing it one PC had already voted to brand another PC as an arch-traitor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This doesn't match my experience when running Celestials games from scratch (unlike the current one where I'm the second GM to run it); IME it's often like herding cats until you get a couple of players who are on the same wavelength. </div> </div> </div>Okay, to be a bit more exact: what I've seen in Celestial games, is that Celestials turn up, most of them get on well, some of them don't and get killed/retired. At the beginning, they get on badly but after a while most of them get on pretty well. Not always all of them but most of them generally. The only issue is that when you introduce new characters, the same thing can happen again.<br /> Well, that's what happened in the game I ran. The game you run, during the time of the previous ST, we all got on pretty well. No one worked against each other (except for the occasional limit break) or drove characters out or whatever.<br /> <br /> DBs, or rather Dynasts, tend to stick together but not really like each other or want to help each other very much, and may well do things behind the scenes (or blatantly) to screw each other over.<br /> I think it probably helps to be in the Threshold for a long time, because you're away from Dynastic politics, where the houses pull you apart.<br /> <br /> To be honest, it probably depends on the players and characters. Obviously some players never play well with others, and some characters will inherently clash (say, if you have a Linowan and a Haltan, or a pacifist and a warlord). But there's nothing particularly inherent to being a Solar, that will drive them apart (besides certain limit breaks I suppose). Whereas with Dynasts, you have Realm politics to drive them apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-14-2014, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T11:12:04-07:00","id":90985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90725#post90725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's an inherent implication in this whole thread that combat is a significant portion of play time. I have been in sessions of Exalted where no combat occurred at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think combat, generally, is an inherent part of RPGs as a form. Obviously there can be sessions, stories, campaigns, and whole groups that never roll out combat. However, I think most groups do have combat regularly.<br /> <br /> The reason I bring up combat is not only is it a significant part of gaming itself, but that Exalted combat, as a system, is bloated and frequently takes way, way too long. This is particularly true of game groups that do not play Exalted exclusively. The system mastery required to run Exalted combat is very high, and I would like it if there was a way to tone those requirements down. That's also why Root's suggestion that any Solar can get extra action charms isn't a solution, but an aggravating element because those charms make combat take way, way too long.<br /> <br /> I want to be able to run Exalted with a group that traditionally plays D&amp;D. That's just not possible at present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the bigger problem is really that 2e is so bad of a system that if you play it the way being implied - isolated character creation, frequent combats - you're left in a situation where, unless absolutely everyone has close to perfect system mastery, there are a billion traps to fall into in terms of creating wide power gaps, and those power gaps will matter excessively, because anytime combat happens it's going to take forever to resolve. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the problem is not in one system, but the cumulative effect of multiple factors all playing together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...in the hands of a halfway competent ST.<br /> <br /> There is very little accounting for bad STs in any of this. </div> </div> </div>One problem is that STing Exalted requires a great deal of system mastery, more than the system mastery required to run most other RPGs. The bar for a competent ST is much higher than a competent D&amp;D DM. This is in part because a new D&amp;D DM can (and probably should) start at level one where there is a limited set of abilities and such with which to contend. In Exalted, the mechanics gates are fewer so it is much easier to create a new, complicated character in Exalted than it is in D&amp;D. I stress that this is a concern of system mastery, as distinguished from general GM mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":1338,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","user":"BvBPL","date":". 03-14-2014, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T11:36:00-07:00","id":90999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90756#post90756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fair enough, but by the time I started playing it one PC had already voted to brand another PC as an arch-traitor.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the traitorous character was played by a player who'd joined the game after the initial bonding was over (he wasn't part of the Sworn Brotherhood that was formed out of the guys just back from the Threshold, for instance), and it's not as if the branding of him as an archtraitor had that much of an effect on him at the time it occured (there was a civil war on, and he had more important things to worry about than reputational damage).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90756#post90756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, it probably depends on the players and characters. Obviously some players never play well with others, and some characters will inherently clash (say, if you have a Linowan and a Haltan, or a pacifist and a warlord). But there's nothing particularly inherent to being a Solar, that will drive them apart (besides certain limit breaks I suppose). Whereas with Dynasts, you have Realm politics to drive them apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I'd like to see in 3E is an emphasis on the importance of Sworn Brotherhoods in the Dynasty -- they were something that the Empress encouraged in order to stop the Realm fragmenting completely, and on a PC party level they're an important counterweight to the tendency of Dynastic politics to pull groups apart. But almost every player I've run into seems to think of House loyalties as primary to personal ones [1]. In fairness, that's what the Houses officially think should be the case, but Dynasts are going to be loyal to their friends over their Houses regardless of what the Houses want to think is the case: one reason that the Houses would emphasise the narrative of loyalty to family above all others is because people are constantly being more loyal to ties other than their family ones... Having this dichotomy between what those in power claim should be the case and what actually happens should be mentioned, I think (it's also a case where that kind of dichotomy, which is characteristic of the Realm, is most likely morally neutral as opposed to problematic, interestingly).<br /> <br /> [1] I don't, but I'm a professional weirdo whose characters tend to take things like SB Oaths seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T11:51:40-07:00","id":91011,"title":"","content":"The problem is that most people play rpgs with combat in mind, with everything else kind of there to make them better at combat. Other rpgs give different classes a different role in combat withe the occasional non-combat supplemental skill. Exalted, on the other hand, just gives one class out of five the &quot;be awesome at fighting&quot; role while the other four do things you kind of just gloss over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1970-yeangst","name":"yeangst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T11:59:54-07:00","id":91013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yeangst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=91011#post91011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that most people play rpgs with combat in mind, with everything else kind of there to make them better at combat. Other rpgs give different classes a different role in combat withe the occasional non-combat supplemental skill. Exalted, on the other hand, just gives one class out of five the &quot;be awesome at fighting&quot; role while the other four do things you kind of just gloss over.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, I'm firmly against declaring badwrongfun, but that said: if you're coming at it from the mindset that &quot;all these other abilities are just here to facilitate combat&quot; then...yeah, Exalted hasn't really been designed with you in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T13:21:25-07:00","id":91045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BvBPL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90985#post90985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's also why Root's suggestion that any Solar can get extra action charms isn't a solution, but an aggravating element because those charms make combat take way, way too long.<br /> <br /> I want to be able to run Exalted with a group that traditionally plays D&amp;D. That's just not possible at present.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I wasn't exactly suggesting that everyone pick up Charms that slow combat to a crawl - I was only pointing out that every caste can, since anima powers are the only real difference between castes. But yes, that would extend the problem, not solve it. I probably talked over my real points, which were that (1) 2E combat is the real problem and (2) the errata help level the playing field a bit. If you want a simpler game, try banning flurries and extra action Charms as well. You'll have to be a little more careful with encounter building. Which D&amp;D version does your group play, btw?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T13:30:28-07:00","id":91054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=91013#post91013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, I'm firmly against declaring badwrongfun, but that said: if you're coming at it from the mindset that &quot;all these other abilities are just here to facilitate combat&quot; then...yeah, Exalted hasn't really been designed with you in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably true. I like to read Exalted books, but I've never actually played a game of it.<br /> <br /> But think about all the video games that exist. What percentage of them revolve around combat? 75%? 80% It'd might have been even higher than 90% if it weren't for games like flappy birds or Candy Crush Saga. Violence is just more exciting, and taboo in real life, which is why we're always trying to simulate it. Don't get me wrong: I enjoyed playing Roller Coaster Tycoon and Startopia, but all most every other game I've ever played revolves around combat. In fact, every play by post Exalted game I've read revolves around combat. The combat system is the core of nearly every table top rpg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1970-yeangst","name":"yeangst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T15:11:46-07:00","id":91127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90108#post90108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentially, it's quite fascinating how so many groups have it easier to assemble a ragtag band of murderhobos from bumfuck nowhere into a party than create a group of peers sharing common background in a highly organized, very social culture. I've seen that problem come up with both versions of Vampire, as well as Legend of the Five Rings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it confuses the hell out of me.<br /> <br /> In my experience Dragon-Blooded characters are <i>way easier</i> to explain as a working party because there are a ton of story-hooks prepared for explaining how they meet each other (primary school, secondary school, family, youthful adventuring, various institutions they can all work for, etc). They have an intricate society and an empire full of interesting crises to solve to explain their group purpose.<br /> <br /> Solar characters could be from anywhere. The party may well lack a single common tongue or culture, they will almost certainly lack any shared history. Due to how their castes are separated into duties as opposed to elemental aspects, a Solar Circle may well not even share any interests either which can make piecing together a cohesive group motivation beyond &quot;mutual self-defense&quot; difficult. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yeangst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=91054#post91054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's probably true. I like to read Exalted books, but I've never actually played a game of it.<br /> <br /> But think about all the video games that exist. What percentage of them revolve around combat? 75%? 80% It'd might have been even higher than 90% if it weren't for games like flappy birds or Candy Crush Saga. Violence is just more exciting, and taboo in real life, which is why we're always trying to simulate it. Don't get me wrong: I enjoyed playing Roller Coaster Tycoon and Startopia, but all most every other game I've ever played revolves around combat. In fact, every play by post Exalted game I've read revolves around combat. The combat system is the core of nearly every table top rpg.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been part of a fairly steady Exalted play-by-post for nearly two years. Fighting has made up less than 1% of the game; aside from a duel to settle a dispute of honor, there's been little need for combat rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T21:00:52-07:00","id":91370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One thing I'd like to see in 3E is an emphasis on the importance of Sworn Brotherhoods in the Dynasty </div> </div> </div> Sounds like a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T00:32:54-07:00","id":91456,"title":"","content":"Clearly the OP has never played D&amp;D. You don't need a cleric. You don't even need a healer. In fact, healing in combat is a terrible thing to do to your allies, because there were at least a half-dozen more useful things you could have used that action for, and they need you to support the team, not waste time. [/tangent]<br /> <br /> I personally hate &quot;everyone has a niche&quot; syndrome, because it leads to &quot;oh, a social encounter, I'll go sit in a corner and knit, and next time, when it's a crafting/sorcery challenger, I'll do stuff and you two can play patty cake next door.&quot; The whole &quot;take turns being allowed to actually do things&quot; set-up is terrible.<br /> <br /> Seriously, don't niche. I really like the Night-Caste crafter who spent all his time on building a (well hidden) factory cathedral. He did what he wanted to, not what his caste dictated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2438-satori","name":"Satori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T00:57:28-07:00","id":91469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=91456#post91456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly the OP has never played D&amp;D. You don't need a cleric. You don't even need a healer. In fact, healing in combat is a terrible thing to do to your allies, because there were at least a half-dozen more useful things you could have used that action for, and they need you to support the team, not waste time. [/tangent]</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahem. Tangent that needs to be addressed: Depends on the edition. His argument is pretty true of 2nd, and to a lesser extent, 1e. You're right when it comes to 3.x. When it comes to 4e, the &quot;dedicated&quot; healers can heal and &quot;do something useful&quot; without wasting actions and some heal *and* do something useful in the same action. In PF, it comes down to class, feat, and archtype selection. 5e/Next I have little experience with/interest in, so I am unqualified to comment.<br /> <br /> In regards to the actual topic of discussion: Like many situations, it seems to be a table issue less than a system issue. Personally, I don't care which splat, I'd like to see mechanics that rely on/work better with others of the same splat. Given their history, DBs would have a slight edge here. But I'd like to see more teamwork oriented mechanics because it gives a mechanical reward for teamwork instead of throwing disparate characters together and hoping their niches line up so everything is covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","name":"Ariketh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T01:32:18-07:00","id":91481,"title":"","content":"I find in practice DB cooperative charms are great in theory but pretty poor in practice. The upgrade for the perfect parry is really good, but you need lots of people to take it and no-one does. The skill upgrading excellency again seems good, but rarely gets used, because people's own abilities are generally good.<br /> Elemental Bolt can put out huge damage, especially if the shot is led by an Earth Aspect. It's incredibly brutal with an elemental lense. But shooting one, expensive, incredibly powerful attack is pretty poor in 2nd ed, even when it does over 100 damage. I think I've only ever seen it actually used like that against things like skyships, since characters can dodge. And all you've done is all used your actions and a decent amount of motes to make one guy spend 8m on a perfect dodge.<br /> <br /> I would definitely like to see them have more, and more useful, cooperative charms in <i>Dragonblood: What Fire Has Wrought</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-15-2014, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T02:38:21-07:00","id":91502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=91456#post91456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly the OP has never played D&amp;D. You don't need a cleric. You don't even need a healer. In fact, healing in combat is a terrible thing to do to your allies, because there were at least a half-dozen more useful things you could have used that action for, and they need you to support the team, not waste time. [/tangent]</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some encounters where healing is useless. There are some encounters where healing is necessary. There are some encounters where healing helps, but isn't necessary.<br /> <br /> If you have a DM who designs small range of encounters, then you may have never been in a situation where healing is important.<br /> <br /> For example: Enemies have been alerted to your group's presence. They wait in room with a ready action of 'open fire at anyone entering.' Your fighter opens the door and half-a-dozen archers and two wizards immediately attack with arrows and color sprays, so said fighter is now down to half health and is dazed*, and it's not even the first round of combat.<br /> <br /> A healer can restore that fighter's HP, give him a buff to defense for one round, and grant him a free saving throw against being dazed with a +3 bonus to the roll, all in one turn.<br /> <br /> This is easily the difference between 'the fighter dies in the first round of combat' and 'the fighter immediately recovers and charges to the group of archers.'<br /> <br /> * Being dazed means your enemies get +2 to attack you, and you can only take one action a turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-15-2014, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T03:02:34-07:00","id":91511,"title":"","content":"It may be helpful to the OP to point out some comparisons between D&amp;D and Exalted, but I suggest we not waste any more internets on discussing the flaws of D&amp;D. There are already entire websites dedicated to that fruitless goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T03:35:36-07:00","id":91523,"title":"","content":"In 4th ed, we've always found that having a Leader to heal people is essential. Probably the most essential class. You can do without a striker (combat is slooow) or a Defender (combat is fast but extremely brutal for your side as well as the other) but you absolutely cannot do without a Leader.<br /> <br /> In 3rd ed things worked pretty differently, but you'd still be in trouble without a Healer, though less so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T08:51:31-07:00","id":91666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=91045#post91045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which D&amp;D version does your group play, btw?</div> </div> </div> </div>3.5 or 4e, depending on the group. 2e was a long, long time ago.<br /> <br /> 3.5 and 4e were designed to expend a certain amount of party resources each combat. In both cases, there was an assumption that the party would have a healer. The combat balancing, in terms of monster level and encounter level and what not, is based around that assumption. That's another great example of how the rules system affects party balance,<br /> <br /> Of course groups can play with this. It is quite possible to have a party of all wizards or something with no healing. However, that requires the whole group, players and DM, working together to overcome the system's assumption of having a healer, which likely means rethinking loot to give more healing potions as well as monster fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T16:05:08-07:00","id":93880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BvBPL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=91666#post91666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3.5 and 4e were designed to expend a certain amount of party resources each combat. In both cases, there was an assumption that the party would have a healer. The combat balancing, in terms of monster level and encounter level and what not, is based around that assumption. That's another great example of how the rules system affects party balance,<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>3e was essentially unplaytested, and it's mechanics resembled the intentions of the writers only tangentially, if at all. Trying to play 3.5 the way the book claims (which mind you, even the authors have by now admitted was terrible lies) you should results in party member deaths if not TPK the moment you run into any of the hundreds of monsters which are under CRed. or any Dragon.<br /> <br /> If you bother to read the late game splats for 3.5, the authors do a much better job, because they have several years worth of gameplay feedback, and the classes are designed to actually work with the mechanics of 3e. Free healing out of combat is basically considered okay by level 6, while in combat healing is more or less acknowledged to be something that you can't afford to spend your standard action on, which is why non-action and swift action heals become common.<br /> <br /> in 4e, the authors, bless them, had long since figured out that no one wants to be a bandaid, and made it possible for every class to at least self-heal. You do need a LEADER in the party, but that's not necessarily a healer - the primary job of the Leader types is Buffing, not healing.<br /> <br /> [/D&amp;D]<br /> <br /> If we could get back to exalted, I am still wondering if anyone had any thoughts about whether niches and niche-protection are actually a desirable thing. My gaming group doesn't really think so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2438-satori","name":"Satori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T16:32:59-07:00","id":93910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=93880#post93880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we could get back to exalted, I am still wondering if anyone had any thoughts about whether niches and niche-protection are actually a desirable thing. My gaming group doesn't really think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, generally. The purpose of niches is (usually) to ensure that every member of a group has something to contribute to the group's efforts, because they have important, non-overlapping skillsets. Niches really only matter in party-based games (which D&amp;D is intended to be), and niche-oriented challenges can be overcome with a little creativity, even in those. I think it's better to build a system around the assumption that every character can, at least to some extent, play solo, and trust that players are intelligent enough to cooperate without a forced mechanical reason for relying on each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T17:32:31-07:00","id":93946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=93880#post93880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we could get back to exalted, I am still wondering if anyone had any thoughts about whether niches and niche-protection are actually a desirable thing. My gaming group doesn't really think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would niche-less Solars look like? The anima powers for the Solars are related to their niches. <br /> <br /> I could see a system whereby we keep the current Solar anima powers, but lose any favored or caste abilities. Just make all abilities a flat rate for every Solar.<br /> <br /> That could go a ways towards balancing everything. STs would still need to work to keep some balance in abilities though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T18:29:06-07:00","id":93989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BvBPL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=93946#post93946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would niche-less Solars look like? The anima powers for the Solars are related to their niches.<br /> <br /> I could see a system whereby we keep the current Solar anima powers, but lose any favored or caste abilities. Just make all abilities a flat rate for every Solar.<br /> <br /> That could go a ways towards balancing everything. STs would still need to work to keep some balance in abilities though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are 2nd Ed. Solars really niche? I generally think of niches as roles with mutually exclusive abilities - in D&amp;D, for instance, there's no way a fighter will ever cast spells without multiclassing, and a wizard by default has terrible attack and durability. They can't really fill in each other's parts.<br /> <br /> I know Solars have caste abilities and anima powers that would tend to make them develop in a particular direction, but technically a Dawn can do almost anything a Twilight can do - it just costs more experience points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 03-18-2014, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T18:35:03-07:00","id":93994,"title":"","content":"Niche-less Solars would just be impossibly amazing at everything, I guess!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T18:53:01-07:00","id":94605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=93989#post93989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are 2nd Ed. Solars really niche? I generally think of niches as roles with mutually exclusive abilities - in D&amp;D, for instance, there's no way a fighter will ever cast spells without multiclassing, and a wizard by default has terrible attack and durability. They can't really fill in each other's parts.<br /> <br /> I know Solars have caste abilities and anima powers that would tend to make them develop in a particular direction, but technically a Dawn can do almost anything a Twilight can do - it just costs more experience points.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> (actually, D&amp;D wizards are much better at fighting than fighters in 3e, but that's due to design issues)<br /> <br /> What i meant by niches is what i talked about in my first post. One of my friends has stopped playing most WW games because he complains that he feels like the games are set up as badly done eigenplots. Oh, a combat encounter, Player X can shine, while player Y works on his knitting. Next, a social encounter. Player Y gets to do stuff, while Player X takes a nap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2438-satori","name":"Satori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T07:11:52-07:00","id":95589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90224#post90224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of that stems from the fact that the society you describe, especially L5R, has very specific expectations of duties from each of the different houses and clans, which many times do not mesh well, or at all, with others. F'rex, it's very difficult to come up with a reason for a Lion, Unicorn, Scorpion, Dragon, and Mantis to work together in anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in my experience, this has more to do with the players. In order to have a cohesive party of characters from a complex interconnected society that takes advantage of those connections to add richness to the experience, everyone has to have a considerable shared understanding of the setting. If one guy is really into Exalted and knows everything there is to know about the Dynasty, but another guy is just kind of casual about it and doesn't want to do all the homework, those two can't meaningfully utilize the background. Conversely, anyone can make a murderhobo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T08:46:42-07:00","id":95674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=90032#post90032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the OP:<br /> I actually find Solars work better as a party together than Dragonblood, most of the time. Not for reasons of power or skillset, but for fluff reasons. The Solars have to work together because of the Wyld Hunt, plot, etc, and also because they're so rare they're the only ones who have things in common with each other, and often end up making friends with each other. There's generally no particular reason why they should not like each other, unless they come from diametrically opposed cultures.<br /> Whereas in most Dragonblood games (though not all) the PCs are Dynasts from different houses. And those houses often spy on each other, compete, clash, and if you're running the Civil War (which I imagine is in a fair few DB games) they could end up on opposite sides, which makes the PCs clash. I've never had a Solar or Lunar killed or driven from the party by another party member, I have had DBs killed, or driven out of the party, by other party members.<br /> And more generally, most of the Celestial parties I've seen, while not everyone always has got on, have been a lot better at working together than the DB parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>In-party conflict is more dramatic and memorable than someone retiring their Dawn because the Night is in every way the superior combatant.<br /> I've done that before and given the group a vague explanation about group dynamics because I didn't want to single out another player and tell them that they were responsible for ruining my fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T15:41:04-07:00","id":96003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BvBPL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=91666#post91666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3.5 or 4e, depending on the group. 2e was a long, long time ago.<br /> <br /> 3.5 and 4e were designed to expend a certain amount of party resources each combat. In both cases, there was an assumption that the party would have a healer. The combat balancing, in terms of monster level and encounter level and what not, is based around that assumption....</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=93880#post93880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3e was essentially unplaytested, and it's mechanics resembled the intentions of the writers only tangentially, if at all....<br /> <br /> If we could get back to exalted, I am still wondering if anyone had any thoughts about whether niches and niche-protection are actually a desirable thing. My gaming group doesn't really think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really have to agree with Satori here. If you only played 4E, I could get that you've been spoiled by a game that is a little harder to break. But 3.5 has just about every problem that Exalted 2E has: much longer turns for some PCs, large disparities in power from one PC to the next, numerous abilities that preemptively end encounters, and player-versus-DM/ST optimization arms races. I'm not saying this to cast doubt or to disparage your complaints though. What have you done, in terms of house rules or agreements (possibly implicit) to make 3.5 work out for you? A lot of the same thinking can help get around the problems in Exalted.<br /> <br /> Regarding Satori's question about niches and niche protection go, I agree that scene-by-scene spotlight balance isn't great. As important as it is for the rules to let us, you know, make our characters as we imagine them, we shouldn't easily become &quot;social-encounter-only guy&quot; or &quot;combat-or-texting gal.&quot; One of the things I like about Ex3 is the promise of easier entry into a type of play: if one or two Charms suffice to make you competent at a task, then there's less incentive to hyper-specialize, dominate encounters of your chosen type, and look for something else to do when it's another player's turn to take 17 actions or mind control a city or single-handedly manage an empire via abstract subsystems. Viable dabbling is really important, and it generally makes the game better for everyone. Winning an encounter alone is cool maybe once in a great while, but collaborating effectively - even without perfectly balanced contributions - is for me the best thing about RPGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T02:31:08-07:00","id":96251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/89555-dragon-bloods-work-better-as-a-party-than-solars-or-the-inverse-cleric-problem?p=96003#post96003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I really have to agree with Satori here. If you only played 4E, I could get that you've been spoiled by a game that is a little harder to break. But 3.5 has just about every problem that Exalted 2E has: much longer turns for some PCs, large disparities in power from one PC to the next, numerous abilities that preemptively end encounters, and player-versus-DM/ST optimization arms races. I'm not saying this to cast doubt or to disparage your complaints though. What have you done, in terms of house rules or agreements (possibly implicit) to make 3.5 work out for you? A lot of the same thinking can help get around the problems in Exalted. Regarding Satori's question about niches and niche protection go, I agree that scene-by-scene spotlight balance isn't great. As important as it is for the rules to let us, you know, make our characters as we imagine them, we shouldn't easily become &amp;quot;social-encounter-only guy&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;combat-or-texting gal.&amp;quot; One of the things I like about Ex3 is the promise of easier entry into a type of play: if one or two Charms suffice to make you competent at a task, then there's less incentive to hyper-specialize, dominate encounters of your chosen type, and look for something else to do when it's another player's turn to take 17 actions or mind control a city or single-handedly manage an empire via abstract subsystems. Viable dabbling is really important, and it generally makes the game better for everyone. Winning an encounter alone is cool maybe once in a great while, but collaborating effectively - even without perfectly balanced contributions - is for me the best thing about RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, thank you. I really hope ex3 does do what you said. On thing that could be interesting is charms that work across multiple competences- eg. They can be useful in both social and physical struggles. In 2e, I think only Sids and GSP's get anything like that, and not easily or effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2438-satori","name":"Satori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}